course: dictionary
lesson: 2620
title: Letters and words that go below the line
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A descender is a noun. In writing, it is the part of a lower-case letter that goes below the line the letters sit on. «Tall parts of letters (b, d, h) are ascenders; tails below the line (g, p, y) are descenders.» The line the letters sit on is called the baseline.
explain: Use the clue in the sentence: a tail that hangs below the line is a descender. «Small ones like a, c, e sit between the lines; tall ones like b, d, h reach up (ascenders); tails like g, p, y hang below the line (descenders).» So a, c and e sit neatly between the lines and have no descender.
explain: Descender has other meanings too. A person or thing that goes down can be a descender, such as «a fast descender», a cyclist or skier who is quick going downhill. In climbing, a descender is a metal device that controls how fast you go down a rope.
fact: A descender is the part of a lower-case letter that goes below the line.
fact: The letters g, j, p, q and y have descenders.
fact: Ascenders go up and descenders go down, and both help readers see the shape of a word.
fact: «A fast descender» means a cyclist or skier who goes down quickly.
fact: In climbing, a descender is a metal device that controls your speed going down a rope.
exercise: Which of these letters has a descender? | h | d | *p | b
exercise: In «a fast descender», what does descender mean? | A tall letter part like the top of b | A letter that sits between the lines | *A cyclist or skier who goes down quickly
exercise: Which letter sits between the lines and has no descender? | p | y | *a | g
test: Where does the descender of the letter g go? | *Below the line | Above the line | Between the lines | On the line
test: Ella holds a metal device on a rope that controls her speed going down. What is it called? | A synonym | *A descender | A baseline | An ascender
exam: Which two letters are descenders in the word «happy»? | b and d | h and a | *p and y | a and c
